        "target-build"
      ],
      "supported_targets": [
        "arduino:renesas_uno:unor4wifi"
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Exact UNO R4 evidence covers GATT write/read/notify, provider disconnect, quiesce/remount/recovery, and an active subscribed link across WiFiS3 DNS/TCP traffic.",
        "One-service, one-characteristic, 20-byte peripheral contract over ArduinoBLE's global HCI/GATT state.",
        "The exact controller artifact establishes 1,180,064 B application flash, 64,628 B static RAM, and 22,288 B / three-task source minima; retained/transient heap, complete task/stack reservations, CPU, and the complete shared-controller price remain unmeasured."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "adapter-wireless-ble-arduino-esp",
      "primary_domain": "wireless",
      "name": "arduino-esp",
      "kind": "adapter",
      "path": "core/adapters/wireless/ble/arduino-esp",
      "deployment": "firmware",
      "maturity": "implemented",
      "evidence": [
        "host-test",
        "physical",
        "target-build"
      ],
      "supported_targets": [
        "esp32:esp32:esp32",
        "esp32:esp32:esp32c3",
        "esp32:esp32:esp32s3"
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Classic ESP32 uses Bluedroid; ESP32-C3/S3 use NimBLE. Exact physical GATT/lifecycle/WiFi coexistence is established for classic ESP32 and ESP32-C3. C3 has a scoped BLE increment; classic ESP32 has an honest whole-composition price because its wifi0 baseline is not separately priced.",
        "One-service, one-characteristic, four-event fixed-ring peripheral contract over the BLE library bundled with Arduino-ESP32 3.3.10."
      ]
    },
